The content rules methods (`getRules`, `createRule`, `deleteRules`) now require a contextual `path` argument, consistent with the other contextual endpoints (the site root is passed as `/`). `deleteRules` now takes `{ path, ruleIds }` instead of a raw `data` object. `updateRules` and its raw `form.button.*` payload were removed in favor of the semantic methods (`enableRules`, `disableRules`, `applyRulesToSubfolders`, `unapplyRulesToSubfolders`, `moveRule`). Also fixed the request body key to `rule_ids` as expected by plone.restapi, and contextual paths are now normalized centrally in the request layer (duplicate slashes collapsed, trailing slashes stripped; embedded query strings are left untouched). The content rules response type was renamed from the misspelled `RuleRespose` to `RuleResponse`. @ArneRiehn
